ther characterize its presentation.", "PTEN:PTEN is a tumor suppressor gene that plays a crucial role in regulating cell growth and apoptosis. It is particularly significant in the context of Cowden syndrome, a genetic disorder characterized by multiple benign tumors and an increased risk of certain cancers. Mutations in the PTEN gene are identified in approximately 80% of cases involving germline mutations associated with Cowden syndrome. This highlights the importance of PTEN in both the diagnosis and understanding of this syndrome.", "PACINI ET AL.:Pacini et al. is a reference cited in the context of the frequency of familial cases of medullary thyroid carcinoma.", "MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA:Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a specific type of thyroid cancer that originates from the parafollicular C cells of the thyroid gland. This cancer is notable for its association with elevated levels of calcitonin, which can be used for diagnosis and monitoring of the disease. Medullary thyroid carcinoma is also linked to certain genetic syndromes, including Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2B (MEN2B) and Cowden syndrome. The disease has the potential to metastasize, making careful monitoring and treatment essential. It is the subject of various studies and clinical trials aimed at improving understanding and management of the condition. At the time of diagnosis, patients may already present with metastases, highlighting the aggressive nature of this cancer.", "GUIDELINES TASK FORCE ON THYROID NODULES AND DIFFERENTIATED THYROID CANCER:This task force is part of the American Thyroid Association and is responsible for developing management guidelines for thyroid conditions.", "SÍNDROME DE COWDEN:El síndrome de Cowden es un síndrome raro de tumores asociado a mutaciones en el gen PTEN. Se caracteriza por la formación de hamartomas en múltiples tejidos y un riesgo aumentado de desarrollar varios tipos de cáncer. Entre los tipos de neoplasias más comunes asociadas con este síndrome se encuentran el cáncer de mama, tiroides y endometrio. Además, el síndrome puede provocar un crecimiento hamartomatoso en tejidos como el colon y la piel.", "TIROIDECTOMÍA:Tiroidectomía is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of all or part of the thyroid gland. It is particularly recommended for patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma, especially in cases where specific mutations, such as those associated with MEN2B, are present. This procedure can have implications for parathyroid hormone levels, potentially affecting the patient's overall hormonal balance.", "LINFADENECTOMÍA CERVICAL:La linfadenectomía cervical es un procedimiento que se debe realizar junto con la tiroidectomía total en el tratamiento del carcinoma medular de tiroides.", "M918T MEN2B:La mutación M918T MEN2B es una mutación genética asociada con un alto riesgo de carcinoma medular de tiroides y requiere cirugía profiláctica antes del primer año de vida.", "GUÍA DE CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES DE LA ATA:La Guía de carcinoma medular de tiroides de la ATA proporciona recomendaciones sobre el manejo y tratamiento de las mutaciones que pueden causar carcinoma medular de tiroides.", "HAMPARTOMAS:Los hamartomas son crecimientos benignos que pueden presentarse en pacientes con síndrome de Cowden, afectando tejidos como colon y piel.", "CALCITONINA:Calcitonin, or \"calcitonina\" in Spanish, is a hormone produced by the C cells of the thyroid gland. It plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body by inhibiting osteoclastic bone resorption, which helps to decrease bone loss. Calcitonin is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as osteoporosis, although its effectiveness in reducing fractures remains a topic of debate. Additionally, it is employed in managing severe hypercalcemia.\n\nThe hormone is also important in the context of medullary thyroid carcinoma, particularly in patients with potential RET mutations. In these cases, calcitonin levels are monitored to assess the risk of developing this type of cancer, as well as to evaluate the progression of the disease and the necessity for surgical intervention. Overall, calcitonin serves both therapeutic and diagnostic purposes in various medical contexts.", "HIPOPARATIROIDISMO:HIPOPARATIROIDISMO, or hypoparathyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone, which results in low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise as a complication following total thyroidectomy and should be considered in surgical management. Additionally, hypoparathyroidism can lead to various complications, including hypomagnesemia and osteoporosis, due to its impact on calcium and phosphate metabolism. The condition may occur due to several factors, including the treatment of thyroid disease and infiltrative diseases that affect the parathyroid glands.", "CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES:", "MEDULLARY THYROID CANCER:Medullary thyroid cancer is a type of thyroid cancer that can be hereditary and is associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia syndromes."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}